+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository: atomic persistence
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, now)` that updates `orders` (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`), inserts the `coupon_redemptions` row, and increments `coupons.used_count`, wrapped in one transaction with rollback on error; verify `npm run build` passes and a focused test shows all three writes appear together.
+- [x] 1.2 Add a focused repository test proving the transaction is all-or-nothing: when a write in the middle fails, the order, `coupon_redemptions`, and `coupons.used_count` are all left unchanged.
+
+## 2. Service: coupon application rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Inject `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` and update the wiring in `src/app.ts`; verify `npm run build` passes and existing tests still pass.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with code normalization (trim + uppercase, REQ-01) and rule checks in the documented error order (`INVALID_REQUEST` → `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` → `ORDER_NOT_PENDING` → `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` → `COUPON_NOT_FOUND` → `COUPON_INACTIVE` → `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID` → `COUPON_EXPIRED` → `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED` → `MINIMUM_NOT_MET`), reading `now` from the injected `Clock`; verify with tests for each error code, the precedence cases (AC-08), the min-amount boundary (AC-06), and the validity window boundaries `now == validFrom` / `now == validUntil` (AC-07), plus `" save20 "` matching `SAVE20` (AC-10).
+- [x] 2.3 Implement the discount computation (FIXED = value; PERCENT = `floor(amount * value / 100)`; `maxDiscountCents` cap; clamp to `amountCents`) and persist it through the repository method; verify with tests for AC-01 through AC-05 and that a successful apply increments `usedCount` and adds one `coupon_redemptions` row (AC-09).
+- [x] 2.4 Verify by test that every rejected request leaves the order amounts, `coupons.used_count`, and `coupon_redemptions` unchanged.
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, delegating to the service; verify an integration test returns HTTP 200 with a body deep-equal to `GET /orders/:id` and a normalized `couponCode` (REQ-14).
+- [x] 3.2 Verify through the route that missing, non-string, and blank `couponCode` bodies return HTTP 400 `INVALID_REQUEST` (REQ-13).
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test`; confirm all pre-existing tests and the new tests pass, and that AC-01 through AC-10 are each covered by a test.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after the project's review requirements are satisfied.
+- Verify the archived result.
